# Time-boxed exception for the pinned ClamAV sidecar image ONLY (ci.yml job
# `clamav-signatures`, ADR-049 § "Temporary exception"). Never used by the
# Rasta service image scans.
#
# CVE-2026-111497 — out-of-bounds write in the Google Brotli decoder
# (brotli-libs). Fixed in brotli-libs 1.2.1-r0, which Alpine 3.24 already
# ships, but the newest upstream clamav/clamav:1.5.4 image (rebuilt
# 2026-10-19, sha256:e19130cd…) still carries 1.2.0-r1, so no digest bump
# closes it. In the pinned image only libcurl depends on brotli-libs, and only
# `freshclam` links libcurl; `clamd`, `clamdscan` and libclamav do not link
# brotli at all (checked with ldd on the pinned digest). Scanned documents
# therefore never reach the vulnerable decoder; exploiting it needs control of
# the HTTPS responses from the signature mirror (database.clamav.net).
# Expires on its own: on 2026-10-31 the scan fails again unless upstream has
# shipped a fixed image (bump the digest) or the exception is re-reviewed.
CVE-2026-111497 exp:2026-10-31
